
1. Microservices Architecture — Top Priority

# 1) What are microservices, and why do we use them?

 Microservices are an architectural style in which a large application is divided into small, independent services, each responsible for a specific business capability.

Each service can be developed, deployed, scaled, and maintained independently, with clearly defined communication between services.

