4. When would you choose each architecture?
Choose a monolith when…

- You are building a new application with a small team.
- The business requirements are still changing rapidly.
- The modules have tightly related business transactions.
- Simpler testing, deployment, and operations are important.

Choose microservices when…

- Different business capabilities need independent releases.
- Different services have substantially different scaling needs.
- Multiple teams can own clear service boundaries.
- Your organization can support distributed monitoring, automation, and failure recovery.


